Selberg factors and period comparisons … Prove unramified calculations and the global unfolding for cuspidal data.' Item 56's note: 'the review should give strong multiplicity one for GL_n one owner.' Also: Item 56: '(Ramakrishnan, arXiv:1806.08429, Theorem A) Isobaric automorphic representations of GL_n(A_E) that agree at the places above almost all primes of F split in E are isomorphic', routed by route 2, with the note '… the review should give strong multiplicity one for GL_n one owner.' PAPER-BEUZARTPLESSIS-CHAUDOUARD-ZYDOR-22/71 (review: accept): 'Ramakrishnan (A theorem on GL(n) à la Tchebotarev, arXiv:1806.08429): … an isobaric automorphic representation of GL_n(A_K) is determined by its local components at the places of K of degree one over F', in its source route to AutomorphicLFunctionsAndLocalFactors, stages ['AutomorphicLFunctionsAndLocalFactors:AL.3']. PAPER-LESLIE-25/95 (review: accept): 'Theorem 9.8 (Ramakrishnan: automorphic Chebotarev density)', also in a source route to AutomorphicLFunctionsAndLocalFactors:AL.3. The paper uses it on pp. 4 and 41 ('by the strong multiplicity one property [Ram, Theorem A]'). Also: Paper p. 3, Definition 1.5: 'Let Π be an isobaric automorphic representation of GL_n(A_E)'. PAPER-BOXER-CALEGARI-GEE-PILLONI-21/335 ('Isobaric sums π_1 ⊞ π_2 for GL_n (Langlands; Jacquet–Shalika)'), status missing, source route to AutomorphicSpectralTheory [AS.1, AS.2, AS.4, AS.5]; its note: 'As the verifier directed, it is routed once, to AutomorphicSpectralTheory (Eisenstein series, AS.1–AS.2)'. RT-PAPER-ALLEN-ETAL-23/21 asks Allen et al. to match the same owner.

findings.claim:
Real representation theory that accepted decisions give to AutomorphicFormsOnReductiveGroups is sent to the AutomorphicSpectralTheory Part II instead:
- Harish-Chandra's discrete-series infinitesimal characters, item 20(a);
- the Langlands classification of irreducible admissible representations of a real reductive group, item 20(b);
- Harish-Chandra's subquotient theorem (subquotient-theorem).
The verifier of RT-AREA-automorphic-1/2 required one owner, and FIX-RT-AREA-automorphic-1 creates AF.1b for exactly these. The confirmed RT-PAPER-NELSON-VENKATESH-21/5 names item 20(b) as a duplicate and says it should import from AF.1b. Route 1 would plan them a second time. Route 1's reason, that real harmonic analysis 'is not planned anywhere and is only needed here', is also out of date:
- NELSON-VENKATESH-21 needs the Plancherel formula, which its accepted verdict assigns to this Part II;
- FIX-RT-AREA-automorphic-1 creates AF.1c for real invariant harmonic analysis. Also: The real-group representation theory inputs of Lemma 2.18 and Proposition 2.24 are routed to route 1 (the Schwartz-multipliers Part II): item 20 (Harish-Chandra's infinitesimal characters of discrete series by Harish-Chandra parameters, the Langlands classification, Knapp's minimal K-types) and the subquotient theorem. The atlas assigns real reductive representation theory to AutomorphicFormsOnReductiveGroups. The confirmed area red-team finding RT-AREA-automorphic-1/2 makes a new stage AF.1b the single owner of Casselman's subrepresentation theorem (which gives the subquotient theorem), the Langlands classification and the discrete series with their Harish-Chandra parameters. Accepted extractions already route discrete series and the archimedean Langlands classification to AF.1. PAPER-NELSON-VENKATESH-21/30 states that item 20(b) here 'plans the same classification and should import it'. Route 1 would build these a second time.

The item is planned only for its non-archimedean and adelic cases. The paper defines I^G_P(σ) for admissible representations of P(R) over any ring R for which admissibility makes sense. §2 uses the real case:
- Lemma 2.25 induces σ_ξ ⊗ τ|_{P_0} from a real minimal parabolic, a representation that is non-trivial on N_0;
- the generic irreducibility of principal series and the subquotient theorem are statements about real principal series;
- Lemma 2.18 uses parabolic induction of discrete series of real Levi subgroups.
Neither planned stage covers this. SR.2 works in the smooth (open-stabiliser) category of p-adic groups, and AS.1 induces from rational parabolics of the adelic group. Normalised parabolic induction of Casselman–Wallach or (g, K) representations of a real group is planned nowhere in the atlas. Also: The item (§1.4: normalised parabolic induction I_P^G(σ) for any ring R 'so that admissibility makes sense') is marked planned at SmoothRepresentationsOfLocalGroups:SR.2 and AutomorphicSpectralTheory:AS.1. Neither plans the archimedean case: SR.2 is the smooth representation theory of reductive groups over nonarchimedean local fields, and AS.1 constructs sections of global induced families from rational parabolics. Section 2 uses induction for the real group G = G(R) throughout: principal series I_{P_0}^G(σ_ξ) from a minimal parabolic of the real group (Lemma 2.25, the subquotient theorem, the proof of (∗)) and standard modules (Lemma 2.18). So the planned item has an unplanned part on the main proof chain of Theorem 2.13.
